 that ",[18,807,808],{},"shouldn't"," flip (a logo always in the top-left, a decorative border).",[53,811,813],{"id":812},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[167,815,816,833,852,871,879],{},[170,817,818,821,822,26,824,26,827,829,830,832],{},[44,819,820],{},"Idiom",": use logical properties (",[23,823,289],{},[23,825,826],{},"padding-inline-end",[23,828,366],{},") for i18n-ready code — they flip automatically in RTL (Arabic, Hebrew) and vertical writing modes, with no ",[23,831,142],{}," overrides. The same CSS works for all languages.",[170,834,835,837,838,154,841,843,844,154,846,848,849,851],{},[44,836,820],{},": use ",[23,839,840],{},"text-align: start",[23,842,164],{}," (not ",[23,845,25],{},[23,847,29],{},") — ",[23,850,161],{}," is left in LTR, right in RTL. This is the logical equivalent for text alignment, and it flips with direction.",[170,853,854,837,856,154,858,843,860,154,862,864,865,867,868,870],{},[44,855,820],{},[23,857,266],{},[23,859,278],{},[23,861,38],{},[23,863,273],{},") for size that should adapt to writing mode — in vertical writing, ",[23,866,266],{}," is the height, ",[23,869,278],{}," is the width. The same CSS works in horizontal and vertical layouts.",[170,872,873,837,875,878],{},[44,874,820],{},[23,876,877],{},"unicode-bidi: isolate"," on embedded user content (names, numbers) in bidirectional text — it prevents LTR numbers\u002Fnames from corrupting the RTL flow. Useful for user-generated content in international apps.",[170,880,881,883,884,886],{},[44,882,820],{},": keep physical properties for things that ",[18,885,808],{}," flip — a logo pinned to the top-left, a decorative gradient direction, a shadow offset. Logical is for flow-relative; physical is for absolute visual effects.",[53,888,890],{"id":889},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[167,892,893,903,928,952,970,981,1006,1024,1035],{},[170,894,895,898,899,902],{},[44,896,897],{},"Browser support",": logical properties are supported in all modern browsers, but very old browsers (IE) don't support them. For IE support, use physical + ",[23,900,901],{},"[dir]"," overrides (or accept IE doesn't get RTL).",[170,904,905,91,911,914,915,918,919,921,922,154,924,927],{},[44,906,907,910],{},[23,908,909],{},"inset"," shorthand",[23,912,913],{},"inset: 0"," (physical, all four sides) vs ",[23,916,917],{},"inset-inline: 0"," (logical, both inline sides). ",[23,920,909],{}," is the physical shorthand; ",[23,923,553],{},[23,925,926],{},"inset-block"," are the logical shorthands.",[170,929,930,941,942,944,945,26,947,944,949,951],{},[44,931,932,154,934,936,937,154,939],{},[23,933,38],{},[23,935,273],{}," vs ",[23,938,266],{},[23,940,278],{},": in horizontal writing mode, ",[23,943,266],{}," = ",[23,946,38],{},[23,948,278],{},[23,950,273],{},". In vertical writing mode, they swap. Mixing physical and logical sizing in the same rule is confusing.",[170,953,954,962,963,154,966,969],{},[44,955,956,154,959],{},[23,957,958],{},"min-inline-size",[23,960,961],{},"max-inline-size",": the logical equivalents of ",[23,964,965],{},"min-width",[23,967,968],{},"max-width"," (in horizontal mode). They exist for all logical properties.",[170,971,972,980],{},[44,973,974,976,977],{},[23,975,349],{}," doesn't flip the ",[18,978,979],{},"color",": the border is on the inline-start edge (which flips), but if you want a different color per side, set them separately.",[170,982,983,992,993,26,995,997,998,1000,1001,26,1003,1005],{},[44,984,985,987,988,154,990],{},[23,986,623],{}," affects ",[23,989,153],{},[23,991,157],{},": with ",[23,994,646],{},[23,996,153],{}," is vertical, ",[23,999,157],{}," is horizontal. Logical properties adapt, but physical properties (",[23,1002,38],{},[23,1004,41],{},") don't — they're always physical.",[170,1007,1008,1013,1014,154,1016,154,1018,1020,1021,1023],{},[44,1009,1010,1012],{},[23,1011,774],{}," doesn't flip everything",": it flips the inline direction (text, inline elements), but ",[23,1015,25],{},[23,1017,29],{},[23,1019,41],{}," are still physical. Use logical properties or ",[23,1022,730],{},"-specific overrides.",[170,1025,1026,1031,1032,1034],{},[44,1027,1028],{},[23,1029,1030],{},"unicode-bidi: plaintext",": infers direction from the content (first strong character). Useful for user input where you don't know the language. ",[23,1033,764],{}," is for embedded content with a known direction.",[170,1036,1037,91,1043,26,1046,1049,1050,944,1053,1055],{},[44,1038,1039,1040],{},"Logical ",[23,1041,1042],{},"border-radius",[23,1044,1045],{},"border-start-start-radius",[23,1047,1048],{},"border-start-end-radius",", etc. — the corners are named by (block, inline). ",[23,1051,1052],{},"border-top-left-radius",[23,1054,1045],{}," in horizontal LTR.",[53,1057,1059],{"id":1058},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[14,1061,1062],{},"A developer makes an RTL-ready card with logical padding, but in RTL the icon is on the wrong side:",[58,1064,1065],{"language":60},[62,1066,1068],{"className":64,"code":1067,"language":60,"meta":66,"style":66},".card { padding-inline-start: 2.5rem; }   \u002F* space for the icon *\u002F\n.card .icon { position: absolute; left: 0.5rem; }  \u002F* icon position *\u002F\n",[23,1069,1070,1090],{"__ignoreMap":66},[70,1071,1072,1074,1076,1078,1080,1083,1085,1087],{"class":72,"line":73},[70,1073,77],{"class":76},[70,1075,639],{"class":80},[70,1077,337],{"class":87},[70,1079,91],{"class":80},[70,1081,1082],{"class":87},"2.5",[70,1084,98],{"class":97},[70,1086,649],{"class":80},[70,1088,1089],{"class":104},"\u002F* space for the icon *\u002F\n",[70,1091,1092,1094,1097,1099,1102,1104,1107,1110,1112,1114,1117,1119,1122],{"class":72,"line":84},[70,1093,77],{"class":76},[70,1095,1096],{"class":76}," .icon",[70,1098,639],{"class":80},[70,1100,1101],{"class":87},"position",[70,1103,91],{"class":80},[70,1105,1106],{"class":87},"absolute",[70,1108,1109],{"class":80},"; ",[70,1111,25],{"class":87},[70,1113,91],{"class":80},[70,1115,1116],{"class":87},"0.5",[70,1118,98],{"class":97},[70,1120,1121],{"class":80},"; }  ",[70,1123,1124],{"class":104},"\u002F* icon position *\u002F\n",[14,1126,1127],{},"What's wrong?",[1129,1130,1131,1135,1152,1155,1205,1219],"details",{},[1132,1133,1134],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1136,1137,1138,1141,1142,1145,1146,1148,1149,1151],{},"The ",[23,1139,1140],{},"padding-inline-start: 2.5rem"," is logical — it flips correctly (padding on the right in RTL, leaving space for the icon on the right). But ",[23,1143,1144],{},".icon { left: 0.5rem; }"," is ",[18,1147,20],{}," — ",[23,1150,25],{}," is always the left side, even in RTL. So in RTL, the padding is on the right (correct), but the icon is on the left (wrong — it should be on the right, where the padding is).",[14,1153,1154],{},"The fix — use a logical inset for the icon:",[62,1156,1158],{"className":64,"code":1157,"language":60,"meta":66,"style":66},".card { padding-inline-start: 2.5rem; }\n.card .icon { position: absolute; inset-inline-start: 0.5rem; }  \u002F* logical *\u002F\n",[23,1159,1160,1176],{"__ignoreMap":66},[70,1161,1162,1164,1166,1168,1170,1172,1174],{"class":72,"line":73},[70,1163,77],{"class":76},[70,1165,639],{"class":80},[70,1167,337],{"class":87},[70,1169,91],{"class":80},[70,1171,1082],{"class":87},[70,1173,98],{"class":97},[70,1175,750],{"class":80},[70,1177,1178,1180,1182,1184,1186,1188,1190,1192,1194,1196,1198,1200,1202],{"class":72,"line":84},[70,1179,77],{"class":76},[70,1181,1096],{"class":76},[70,1183,639],{"class":80},[70,1185,1101],{"class":87},[70,1187,91],{"class":80},[70,1189,1106],{"class":87},[70,1191,1109],{"class":80},[70,1193,366],{"class":87},[70,1195,91],{"class":80},[70,1197,1116],{"class":87},[70,1199,98],{"class":97},[70,1201,1121],{"class":80},[70,1203,1204],{"class":104},"\u002F* logical *\u002F\n",[14,1206,1207,1208,1145,1211,1214,1215,1218],{},"::\nNow ",[23,1209,1210],{},"inset-inline-start: 0.5rem",[23,1212,1213],{},"left: 0.5rem"," in LTR and ",[23,1216,1217],{},"right: 0.5rem"," in RTL — the icon is on the same side as the padding, in both directions.",[14,1220,1221,1224,1225,1227,1228,1231],{},[44,1222,1223],{},"The lesson",": mixing logical (padding) and physical (",[23,1226,25],{},") properties breaks i18n — one flips, the other doesn't, and they get out of sync. Use logical properties ",[18,1229,1230],{},"consistently"," for flow-relative layout (padding, margin, positioning insets). Reserve physical for effects that shouldn't flip (a logo, a fixed shadow).",[53,1233,1234],{"id":1132},"Summary",[14,1236,1237,1238,154,1240,154,1242,154,1244,26,1246,154,1248,26,1250,26,1253,1256,1257,26,1259,1261,1262,154,1264,1266,1267,154,1269,154,1271,1273,1274,1276],{},"You can now use logical properties (",[23,1239,222],{},[23,1241,233],{},[23,1243,244],{},[23,1245,255],{},[23,1247,266],{},[23,1249,278],{},[23,1251,1252],{},"margin-inline-*",[23,1254,1255],{},"inset-inline-*","), shorthands (",[23,1258,520],{},[23,1260,553],{},"), logical text alignment (",[23,1263,161],{},[23,1265,164],{},"), writing modes (",[23,1268,679],{},[23,1270,646],{},[23,1272,666],{},"), and ",[23,1275,877],{}," for bidirectional text — making CSS i18n-ready for RTL and vertical writing. Next: modern CSS features.",[1278,1279,1280],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .snvgF, html code.shiki .snvgF{--shiki-default:#005CC5;--shiki-github-dark:#79B8FF}html pre.shiki code .svdQ7, html code.shiki .svdQ7{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-github-dark:#F97583}html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html.github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html pre.shiki code .sk71V, html code.shiki .sk71V{--shiki-default:#22863A;--shiki-github-dark:#85E89D}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}",{"title":66,"searchDepth":84,"depth":84,"links":1282},[1283,1284,1288,1289,1291,1292,1294,1295,1296,1297,1298],{"id":55,"depth":84,"text":56},{"id":146,"depth":84,"text":147,"children":1285},[1286,1287],{"id":190,"depth":108,"text":191},{"id":369,"depth":108,"text":370},{"id":506,"depth":84,"text":507},{"id":573,"depth":84,"text":1290},"text-align and Logical Values",{"id":617,"depth":84,"text":618},{"id":709,"depth":84,"text":1293},"direction and unicode-bidi",{"id":784,"depth":84,"text":785},{"id":812,"depth":84,"text":813},{"id":889,"depth":84,"text":890},{"id":1058,"depth":84,"text":1059},{"id":1132,"depth":84,"text":1234},"CSS has traditionally been physical (left, right, top, bottom, width, margin-left). Logical properties are flow-relative — they adapt to the writing direction (LTR, RTL, vertical). This is essential for internationalized (i18n) code.","md",{},true,"\u002Fcss\u002F16-logical-properties-and-writing-modes",{"title":5,"description":1299},"css\u002F16-logical-properties-and-writing-modes","NrDHk3Ji-G25MeiPQoPRiMM-a19Vwr2PQLeEJMNgVQI",1787401627499]